RF.put("questb:b27",{"8667":{"id":8667,"t":"Genesis Helm","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nVek'lor's Diadem Emperor Vek'lor in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Life Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The Twin Emperors... their incessant whispers are slowly taking a toll on my sanity. They mock me, knowing I cannot step further into their domain to save my brother Arygos.\nIn my visions I see their monstrous faces adorned by powerful crowns. But I will have my revenge... I will transmute these symbols of Qiraji power to ones better suited to our needs.\nBring me the components I require, ‹name›. I will give you a headpiece of unmatched power.","rew":"You will receive:\nGenesis Helm\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring me the components I asked for, ‹name›?","done":"You've succeeded! The whispers from the Twin Emperors have ceased.\nTake this as a reward. The mere sight of it will strike fear in the hearts of the Qiraji... it shall remind them of their fallen leaders and of the mortal that slew them.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Druid Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8667\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Genesis Helm this quest\nBring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"6827":{"id":6827,"t":"Call of Air - Mulverick's Fleet","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stormpike Commander's Flesh Alliance Sentinel , Stormpike Mountaineer , Frostwolf in Alterac Valley , Irondeep Trogg in Alterac Valley and 4 more","back":"I was locked up in a dwarven hellhole for days. You better believe I want revenge!\nWe must plan carefully.\nFirst, my war riders need targets to gun for - high priority targets. I'm going to need to feed them the flesh of Stormpike Commanders. Unfortunately, those little buggers are entrenched deep behind enemy lines! You've definitely got your work cut out for you.","done":"Not enough! I would expect this level of work from an initiate, but you, ‹name›? Come on, soldier! HUSTLE! More flesh is needed!\nStart Wing Commander Mulverick Alterac Valley End Wing Commander Mulverick Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6827","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"667":{"id":667,"t":"Death From Below","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Protect Shakes O'Breen during the attack.","desc":"This is bad. It seems the Daggerspines are amassing for an attack.\nNaga are known for their ruthlessness in battle. They will keep attacking until I am dead.\nI don't value my own life above that of my crew members, but you must help to defend me. The crew will not be able to make it back to Booty Bay without my knowledge of the seas.\nThe naga will be coming from the sea. I need you to remain up here with me to fend off the attack. Man the cannon and drive them back.\nAre you ready, ‹name›?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nColdwater Ring Seafire Band\nExperience: 4,650\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"We survived the attack!\nWe could not have done it without you, ‹name›.\nWe'll be heading out as soon as the tide rises. If you weren't such a promising hero I'd offer you a place on my crew. But I can tell you have bigger fish to fry.\nEven if you are a puny ‹race›....","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":32.3,"y":81.4,"n":"Shakes O'Breen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"98027":{"id":98027,"t":"Gleaming crescent necklace","lv":29,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Crescent Necklace to Maliynn in Astranaar.\nGleaming Crescent Necklace","desc":"<The silver necklace in your hands gleams gently as you examine it. The small crescent moon shape seems similar to other night elf symbols you've seen before.\nUpon flipping the necklace over there is a small inscription: \"Alor'lormah, Maliynn\". Perhaps it belongs to Maliynn in Astranaar?>","rew":"You will receive:\nReplica Crescent Necklace\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":63,"y":71.5,"n":"Gleaming Crescent Pendant","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.6,"y":49.8,"n":"Maliynn","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"7867":{"id":7867,"t":"Outrider Standard Care Package","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nOutrider Standard Care Package\nExperience: 380\n+10 reputation with Warsong Outriders","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Warsong Gulch.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Gulch, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Friendly with us, and bandages when you are Honored.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.4,"n":"Kelm Hargunth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"8987":{"id":8987,"t":"More Components of Importance","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve a Brilliant Sword of Zealotry and return it to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\nBrilliant Sword of Zealotry Scarlet Praetorian","desc":"‹class›, listen closely. Now that we have the location of the last amulet piece, we still need another component to suffuse the brazier with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to summon the remains of my deceased, former comrades.\nThe siblings, Jarien and Sothos, were believers in the way of the Scarlet Crusade. They aspired to knighthood within that vile organization. Go to Tyr's Hand in Eastern Plaguelands and retrieve a Brilliant Sword of Zealotry from the praetorians there.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n3 Bloodkelp Elixir of Dodging 3 Bloodkelp Elixir of Resistance\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you returned already then, ‹class›, with what I sent you out to gather?","done":"A job well done, ‹name›. I will imbue the essence of the sword into the brazier.\nNow all that is left is to get into The Crimson Throne inside The Scarlet Bastion at Stratholme, and use the brazier to summon forth the remains of my former cohorts, Jarien and Sothos. Their souls have been twisted further by their possession of Valthalak's amulet piece and his spirit within.\nOh, by the way, I had some leftover bloodkelp from your trip to Alcaz Isle, so I made it into some potions for you. Take your pick!\nBurning Steppes Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"4907":{"id":4907,"t":"Tinkee Steamboil","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tinkee Steamboil.","desc":"Hi, ‹name›. Remember Tinkee Steamboil? Well, she remembers you! She sent me a message to keep an eye out for you, because... she needs your help again. I think it has something to do with her studies on dragons.\nYou should speak to her in the Burning Steppes, at the Flame Crest.","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Felnok was right! I do need your help again, and this time... it's going to be really dangerous.\nAre you ready??\nWinterspring Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.6,"y":38.6,"n":"Felnok Steelspring","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.2,"y":24,"n":"Tinkee Steamboil","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"5307":{"id":5307,"t":"Corruption","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,550, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Find the Black Guard Swordsmith in Stratholme and destroy him. Recover the Insignia of the Black Guard and return to Seril Scourgebane.\nInsignia of the Black Guard Black Guard Swordsmith","desc":"If I am short with you, it is for a reason. The plans for the creation of the great blade, Corruption, have been stolen by the Black Guard: Elite skeletal units of Baron Rivendare.\nYes, Baron Rivendare of Stratholme.\nThe Black Guard swordsmith now guards those plans with his... undeath.\nSlay him and return proof of this deed and I shall grant you the knowledge required to create a blazing rapier!","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Blazing Rapier\nExperience: 8,300","back":"Have you forgotten what it is that you were tasked with, ‹name›?","done":"It should be obvious that a sword is always the best choice.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.3,"y":37.2,"n":"Seril Scourgebane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"3627":{"id":3627,"t":"Uniting the Shattered Amulet","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Grol the Destroyer, Lady Sevine, and Archmage Allistarj. From their corpses take the Amulet of Grol, the Amulet of Sevine, and the Amulet of Allistarj.\nRemember to USE your Enchanted Azsharite Fel Weaponry to weaken the triad. They cannot be killed otherwise - but use them wisely...\nAmulet of Allistarj Archmage Allistarj\nAmulet of Grol Grol the Destroyer\nAmulet of Sevine Lady Sevine","desc":"To reach the Defiler, you must first destroy the triad of power and recover the amulet pieces. When you recover all three pieces, return to me and I shall give you further instruction.\nGo ‹name›! To the Blasted Lands! Sevine, Allistarj, and Grol must fall!","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"The three shall form the one, the one shall light the way.","done":"The amulet of Razelikh the Defiler is once again complete but he senses the disruption in his chain of command. He knows you come for him...\nSwamp of Sorrows Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"96987":{"id":96987,"t":"Opportunistic education","lv":33,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect the Founding of Dalaran from the City of Dalaran for Rexxie Copperclutch near the sewer entrance.\nThe Founding of Dalaran","desc":"Well if it ain't a like-minded entrepreneur. Sneakin' into Dalaran durin' such troublesome times? Tsk tsk.\nMy kinda ‹race›!\nWhile our mage friends here are occupied, maybe we could find ourselves some 'misplaced' treasures. They gots whole libraries dedicated to fancy arcane magics. If you could bring me one of their secret tomes, I could sell it for a pretty penny. Split the profits with ya.\nHey hey don't look at me like that. You ain't exactly here on a field trip yourself. You want in or what?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSolid Gold Band Larcenist's Belt\nExperience: 9,400\nWhere to find it Past the portal room, on the back wall. Level 33 , requires level 24 Difficulty 24 29 31 36 42 Side Horde Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 96987","cats":["city-of-dalaran"]},"94347":{"id":94347,"t":"Craftsmans writ wicked leather bracers","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Wicked Leather Bracers\nWicked Leather Bracers","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Wicked Leather Bracers, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Wicked Leather Bracers Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94347","cats":["crafting"]},"94267":{"id":94267,"t":"Craftsmans writ wildvine potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Wildvine Potion\nWildvine Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Wildvine Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Wildvine Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94267","cats":["crafting"]},"1387":{"id":1387,"t":"Centaur Bounty","lv":31,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Centaur Ears to Corporal Melkins at Nijel's Point in Desolace.\n15 Centaur Ear Kolkar Ambusher 20 % , Kolkar Waylayer 20 % , Outcast Necromancer 20 % , Maraudine Khan Advisor 20 % and 4 more","desc":"Many clans make up the centaur race. Each has its own leader and agenda, but all the clans have one thing in common. Cruelty.\nIf we are to ever find peace, then the centaurs must be removed. And so I put you on the task to do just that.\nWhile wandering Desolace, hunt centaur and take their ears. Bring me many, many ears.\nDo this in service of the Alliance, ‹name›, and we will be one step closer to war's end.","rew":"You will receive:\nRing of Calm\nExperience: 3,750\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Do you have a report, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, the ears. Well done.\nYour service to the Alliance is unquestioned, ‹name›. The blood you spilled in Desolace will, no doubt, save countless lives.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.7,"y":10.9,"n":"Corporal Melkins","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"6027":{"id":6027,"t":"Book of the Ancients","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get the Book of the Ancients and return it to Azore Aldamort at the tower in Ethel Rethor.\nBook of the Ancients Lord Kragaru\nGem of the Serpent\nProvided: Gem of the Serpent","desc":"‹name›, I entrust you with the Gem of the Serpent. Place this gem on the Serpent Statue's hand on Ranazjar Isle, a small island northwest of here. Placing it will summon the one who protects the Book of the Ancients. This book contains the secrets of the naga, secrets that have been kept for centuries. Bring this book to me, and we will learn much about our scaled foes!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSilkstream Cuffs Arcmetal Shoulders\nMoney: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,550\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Ah, ‹name›! It's good to see you again. Do you have the Book of the Ancients?","done":"The long lost Book of the Ancients! I will ensure this book is passed on to the high council. You've done well today, and for that you are to be thanked... as a hero should be thanked!","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":38.9,"y":27.2,"n":"Azore Aldamort","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"1467":{"id":1467,"t":"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc.","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Leftwitch's Package back to Roetten Stonehammer in Ironforge.\nLeftwitch's Package\nProvided: Leftwitch's Package","desc":"To get paid, you're gonna have to get back to Ironforge and speak to Roetten himself. He'll love getting Leftwitch's package out of the way anyway. Just give him this and it should be enough to get your booty.\nAnd don't worry, I'm still going to put in a good word for you when I get back. I shouldn't be in Desolace much longer.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAuric Bracers Stormfire Gauntlets\nMoney: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Well met, ‹name›. Business is booming, the sounds of anvils being struck rings throughout Ironforge, the bellows blow the fires hot, and me wife's making me a pie for dessert after tonight's dinner. Could life be any grander?","done":"Ah, the package for Leftwitch from Desolace. Excellent. I 'preciate the work, and your timeliness, ‹class›. Glad to have you aboard for at least this small bit of work.\nI got your payment right here. Let it be known that Reclaimers Inc. always pays well for a hard week's work.\nDesolace Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.2,"y":9.6,"n":"Kreldig Ungor","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":24.5,"n":"Roetten Stonehammer","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"93227":{"id":93227,"t":"Buying friendship gelkis","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Totem Tote to the Gelkis Quartermaster at Gelkis Village in the Desolace to significantly increase your reputation with that clan. You must be of at least Neutral standing with the Gelkis Clan Centaur.\nProvided: Totem Tote","desc":"At first glance, I would wager that the Gelkis are struggling. Their numbers are far fewer than the Magram, and I rarely hear of them stomping around from our scouts.\nNonetheless, they are one of the dominant clans in the Desolace and survive to this day. They must be doing something right.\nIf you want to make peace with the Gelkis, take this tote of totems with you to Gelkis Village far to the southwest. Primitive as they may be, they are likely to have a treasurer of some kind.\nLevel 45 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 41 43 48 57 Side Both factions Quest ID 93227","cats":["desolace"]},"27":{"id":27,"t":"A Lesson to Learn","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.","desc":"‹name›, I have been following your progress with much delight. You are most assuredly developing yourself into a valued protector of nature.\nThe time has come for you to learn more about one of the various animal aspects that Cenarius has blessed us with the ability to change into - one that affords you command and mastery of the water. For this, you must travel to the village of Nighthaven in Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle there. He will guide you further.","rew":"Experience: 120","done":"Salutations, young ‹class›; the time has come for you to know our aquatic form. It is one that lets you move freely and indefinitely through water. You will find this aspect a useful tool and a blessing... but it is one that must be earned before it is mastered.\nYou will face two trials to overcome. The first will test your ability to work in water under pressure. The second will test your resolve to understand the aspects of the form itself.\nStand ready, as the time of testing is now upon us.\nDarnassus Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"827":{"id":827,"t":"Skull Rock","lv":12,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather Searing Collars from the cultists in Skull Rock.\nBring them to Margoz at his camp.\n6 Searing Collar Burning Blade Cultist , Burning Blade Apprentice , Burning Blade Fanatic , Burning Blade Neophyte and 1 more","desc":"‹name›. The Burning Blade has infested the cave east of Orgrimmar known as Skull Rock. Inside that cave they perform vile rituals, and burn their own flesh with Searing Collars.\nBy wearing these collars, I believe the cultists attune themselves to demonic power. But to confirm this, I must have a collection of the collars to study.\nGo to Skull Rock and gather Searing Collars from the cultists you find there. Bring them to me, and I will uncover their secrets.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nJagged Dagger Steady Bastard Sword Stinging Mace\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Have you yet entered Skull Rock, ‹name›? Do you have the Searing Collars?","done":"Good. Hiding within these collars is the secret behind the Burning Blade. And I will uncover that secret...","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":56.4,"y":20,"n":"Margoz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"6187":{"id":6187,"t":"Order Must Be Restored","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Assemble an army and travel to the Eastern Plaguelands. Launch a full assault on Nathanos Blightcaller and any Horde filth that may attempt to protect him.\nKeep your wits about you, ‹name›. The Horde will defend the ranger lord with their very lives.\nNathanos Blightcaller slain","desc":"Do you know how many ranger lords exist in this world? How many human ranger lords have ever existed?\nNathanos' accomplishments were unprecedented. He was a tactical genius, responsible for Alliance victories spanning a decade of conflict.\nAnd now... the champion of the Forsaken.\nNo. This cannot be. Order must be restored.\nGather an army, ‹name›. Return to the Plagues with your army and destroy the Blightcaller.\nI wish you luck, ‹name›. Truly, you will need it for this battle.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGorewood Bow Stormrager Sacred Protector\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"<Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is lost in thought.>","done":"It is a tragedy. I think... I believe that our kind is cursed, ‹name›. We are cursed to lose our greatest warriors; our most noble heroes; our most gifted scholars.\nWe are indebted to you and I assure you, ‹name›, wherever Nathanos Marris is now, he smiles down upon you.\nStormwind City Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9227":{"id":9227,"t":"Superior Armaments of Battle - Exalted Amongst the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"For 6 Insignias of the Dawn and 6 Insignias of the Crusade you may choose an item from the Argent Dawn's treasure cache.\n6 Insignia of the Dawn\n6 Insignia of the Crusade","desc":"Greetings, friend. Have you insignias of the Dawn or the Crusade that you would like to redeem for items of power?\nItems offered to those exalted amongst the Dawn are discounted. I encourage you to make a purchase!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBand of Piety Band of Resolution Verimonde's Last Resort Supply Bag Leggings of the Plague Hunter Sanctified Leather Helm\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Choose carefully. There are no refunds.","done":"Good day, ‹name›. It was a pleasure doing business with you.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.8,"y":50.2,"n":"Quartermaster Miranda Breechlock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"107":{"id":107,"t":"Note to William","lv":6,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Gramma Stonefield's Note to William Pestle.\nGramma Stonefield's Note\nProvided: Gramma Stonefield's Note","desc":"I bet William Pestle has a potion to unite our two young lovers!\nHere, take this note to William. He's staying at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.","rew":"Experience: 140\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have a note from \"Gramma\" Stonefield, eh? I haven't seen Mildred in years! I wonder what she has to say...","done":"My heart goes out to those two poor souls, Maybell and Tommy Joe. I remember being young and in love, once.\nThere must be something I can do to help them! Let me think...","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":34.9,"y":83.9,"n":"Gramma Stonefield","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.3,"y":65.7,"n":"William Pestle","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"4107":{"id":4107,"t":"Salve via Disenchanting","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Lesser Nether Essence","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"The power of a disenchanted magical item is felt by the essence it creates. I've devised a way to turn raw essence used by enchanters into a suitable reagent for creating Cenarion plant salve. You don't need a Cenarion beacon for this; any suitably disenchanted item that yields lesser nether essences will work.\nI just need a single lesser nether essence; in exchange, I will give you Cenarion plant salves. The essence is extremely potent - a little definitely goes a long way!","done":"Here are some Cenarion plant salves - I only need one lesser nether essence for this, ‹name›. Essence is by far the most potent item I can make use of to turn swords into plowshares, as it were. If you need more salve, then find me here!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2987":{"id":2987,"t":"Gordunni Cobalt","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Orwin Gizzmick in Camp Mojache wants 12 samples of Gordunni Cobalt.\n12 Gordunni Cobalt Gordunni Dirt Mound\nOrwin's Shovel\nProvided: Orwin's Shovel","desc":"I just arrived here in Feralas, and I've heard that the Gordunni Ogres that inhabit the wilds here have some interesting minerals. Who knows what they are up to, but they sure are protective of that stuff! They don't leave it just lying around; no, they bury it to protect folks like me from getting their hands on it.\nIf you'd be willing, I'll give you my shovel. Go to the Gordunni Outpost north of here and dig me up some Gordunni cobalt. Look for the blue glow, then start digging!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBoots of the Maharishi Stargazer Cloak\nExperience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Get on up there and start digging!\nI've got places to go and people to see -- time is money!","done":"Perfect! I will take these along as I continue my travels, ‹name›. I'm sure I can find someone that will pay a pretty penny for this cobalt.\nHere, take this for your trouble.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":75.7,"y":44.3,"n":"Orwin Gizzmick","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"4267":{"id":4267,"t":"Rise of the Silithid","lv":46,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Raschal's Report to Gracina Spiritmight in Darnassus.\nRaschal's Report\nProvided: Raschal's Report","desc":"I am entrusting you with a copy of the report Raschal made on the infestation of southeastern Feralas. While the main report is being filed in Darnassus, I want you to give this copy to an associate of the Protectorate. Her name is Gracina Spiritmight; she is a priestess who dwells in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. She has broad knowledge on these kinds of creatures, and her receiving this report would benefit us all.\nYou're dismissed - good luck, ‹name›; may Elune watch over us all.","rew":"Experience: 410","back":"Welcome to this blessed temple, friend. Your arrival here from Feathermoon Stronghold has been foretold to me. Do you have the report Shandris Feathermoon asked you to bring?","done":"We night elves know of the terror outlined in this report. Shandris was wise to send this, and you, to me.\nThese creatures will consume Feralas rapidly; they are nothing short of one of the greatest menaces we all will ever face. The insects you and the courier encountered are known as the silithid. They are mere tools of one of the greatest threats that both the Horde and Alliance will ever face.\nI pray we will have the resolve to defeat them before they destroy us.\nFeralas Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Shandris Feathermoon","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":41.8,"y":85.6,"n":"Gracina Spiritmight","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"97067":{"id":97067,"t":"Tip the scales dezian queenfish","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Dezian Queenfish","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Speckled Tastyfish\nLevel 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 97067","cats":["fishing"]},"507":{"id":507,"t":"Lord Aliden Perenolde","lv":42,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Lord Aliden Perenolde and ask his mistress, Elysa, about Taretha's pendant.\nLord Aliden Perenolde slain","desc":"It is clear that Perenolde must be killed, his foulness removed from the world. His manor lies a ways to the north of here, on the shores of Lordamere Lake. Do your duty, ‹name›, then retrieve the pendant that the Warchief desires, and return here.","rew":"Experience: 4,300","back":"W-what do you want?","done":"No, no please don't hurt me! I never meant your people any harm, he's had me against my will! Please... spare me!\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":63.2,"y":20.7,"n":"Krusk","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.3,"y":14.3,"n":"Elysa","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"8907":{"id":8907,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Magister's Bindings to Deliana in Ironforge.\n15 Winterspring Blood Sample Rabid Shardtooth 30 % , Elder Shardtooth 30 % , Shardtooth Bear 30 % , Shardtooth Mauler 30 % and 4 more\nMagister's Bindings Rage Talon Fire Tongue 3.5 % , Firebrand Pyromancer 1.4 % , Scarshield Spellbinder 1.2 % , Bloodaxe Evoker 1.1 % and 1 more","desc":"Well met, ‹class›. I've something that might interest you.\nI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality. I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.\nThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment. Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold. You shall find the effort worth your while.","rew":"You will receive:\nSorcerer's Bindings\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you brought me what I requested of you, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent! Let's perform the trade then. It's hard to part with this excellent armor, but I'm afraid I won't be needing it any time soon.\nIf you're interested in performing more work for me, I might be willing to give up the rest of the pieces.\nDun Morogh Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"7787":{"id":7787,"t":"Rise, Thunderfury!","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 10,900, 0.91 times as much.","obj":"Present the Dormant Wind Kissed Blade to Highlord Demitrian.\nDormant Wind Kissed Blade Prince Thunderaan\nProvided: Dormant Wind Kissed Blade","desc":"You have defeated the Wind Seeker. Take the dormant blade and force the lying wretch, Demitrian, to use the materials you provided for his betrayal to wake Thunderfury.","rew":"You will receive:\nThunderfury, Blessed Blade of the Windseeker\nExperience: 9,950","back":"<Demitrian cowers in your presence.>","done":"Please do not harm me! Take it! Take the blade! Leave Demitrian to reshape his pathetic life!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":21.7,"y":8.6,"n":"Highlord Demitrian","e":1}],"cats":["legendary"]},"86667":{"id":86667,"t":"Snowbound","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver a Jar of Snow to Norric Lochthane at his house on the northwest coast of the Loch.\nJar of Snow","desc":"My old mentor, Norric, sent a minor elemental with an odd request. He needs a jar of snow for some of his shamanic workings! I don't know what he's going to do with that, but I learned a long time ago not to question his ways with respect to magic.\nI'm busy learning about the local elementals, so I can't leave to help him. Go to the tunnel entrance at South Gate Pass where there's snow year-round. Scoop some up in this ceramic jar and bring it to him before it melts. The jar should keep it cold.","back":"Eh? What do you want?","done":"This jar is for me?\nSnow! Grenhild did it! She sent the snow that I asked for!\nA pity, though, I was hoping she would come and visit in person.\nWell, regardless, thank you for your effort. This is a real help for my work.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":36.4,"y":48.2,"n":"Grenhild Darktalon","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":41.8,"y":19,"n":"Norric Lochthane","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"267":{"id":267,"t":"The Trogg Threat","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Trogg Stone Teeth to Captain Rugelfuss in the southern guard tower.\n8 Trogg Stone Tooth Berserk Trogg 50 % , Stonesplinter Shaman 50 % , Stonesplinter Digger 50 % , Stonesplinter Seer 50 % and 4 more","desc":"‹class›, you may or may not be aware of the Trogg threat looming over Dwarven lands. With the Ironforge Reserve called up to the Alliance Front, we are left with a fraction of the defense forces needed to keep these lands safe. My regiment is assigned to watch over the Gate here and we cannot leave our post for fear of invasion.\nBut we need some pressure put on those damned Troggs lurking in the hills. If you're up to the task, wage an assault on the Troggs. Bring me back 8 Trogg Stone Teeth as proof.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Do you have 8 Trogg Stone Teeth to show me? If not, there is still work to be done, ‹name›.","done":"I am quite impressed, ‹name›. You have done the Dwarven race a great favor by defending our lands. King Magni Bronzebeard himself would be proud!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":23.2,"y":73.7,"n":"Captain Rugelfuss","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"1947":{"id":1947,"t":"Journey to the Marsh","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tabetha.","desc":"Now it is time for you to earn your mage's wand. To begin this quest, speak with the human hermit Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh. You will find her shack deep in the marsh, west of Theramore.\nSpeak with her, for her knowledge is vast. You will find Tabetha's cottage west of Theramore, and just north of the Stonemaul Ruins.","rew":"Experience: 290","done":"Quiet! I'm in a delicate juncture and mustn't be disturbed!\nOne moment...\nStormwind City Orgrimmar Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":85.8,"n":"Jennea Cannon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.4,"y":86.1,"n":"Deino","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"7067":{"id":7067,"t":"The Pariah's Instructions","lv":48,"min":39,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Pariah's Instructions. Afterwards, obtain the Amulet of Union from Maraudon and return it to the Centaur Pariah in southern Desolace.\nAmulet of Union\nProvided: The Pariah's Instructions","desc":"Though exiled as a heretic, my beliefs still ring true--that alone drives me onward. But for my destiny to be complete, I need the aid of an outsider... one not of any centaur tribe.\nThe task requires someone to enter the holy halls of Maraudon--a tomb my people protect, and only the most devout are ever allowed to enter.\nIf you agree to aid me, then you need only nod. I will pass you a parchment with my instructions on it. Read it over and consider my words.","rew":"You will receive:\nMark of the Chosen\nMoney: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,450","back":"What did you decide, ‹name›? Can you help me? Will you set foot on holy ground to help me forge one great centaur tribe!?","done":"This is it, ‹race›! This is it! Now I can begin the great task of uniting the tribes. Thank you.\nTake this for your efforts, please. I hope when next we meet, it will be on much different terms.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":50.4,"y":86.7,"n":"Centaur Pariah","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["maraudon"]},"747":{"id":747,"t":"The Hunt Begins","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Grull Hawkwind in Camp Narache wants you to bring him 7 Plainstrider Feathers and 7 pieces of Plainstrider Meat.\n7 Plainstrider Meat Plainstrider 80 %\n7 Plainstrider Feather Plainstrider 80 %","desc":"You have a promising air about you, and will prove yourself to the tribe. Perhaps someday soon you will be welcomed into the great city of Thunder Bluff. But before that can happen you must prove yourself to my father, Chief Hawkwind.\nUp here on Red Cloud Mesa we pride ourselves on keen hunting skills. Tauren hunt out of necessity and for sport. Our supply of meats has run low and we require feathers for clothing. Hunt the nearby plainstriders and prove yourself by resupplying the village.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nNomadic Belt Painted Chain Gloves\nExperience: 170\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Providing meat and feathers for the tribe is the first step in proving yourself as a ‹class› before the Chief.","done":"The Tauren of Narache thank you, ‹name›. You show much promise.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.5,"y":77.5,"n":"Grull Hawkwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"98427":{"id":98427,"t":"Ceasing operations","lv":12,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Clearcutter Key to Morin Cloudstalker outside Bloodhoof Village.\nClearcutter Key","desc":"The shredder one of the pages speaks of--I have seen them before in my travels. They can decimate a forest in a fraction of the time that hand and axe can.\nEntire glades--homes to the Earth Mother's children for millenia--erased in days.\nWe will not allow this to happen in our home, a stone's throw from where our young ones take their first steps.\n‹name›, I must ask you to gather others, go back into the mine to the northeast, and ensure it fells not a single tree more.","rew":"You will receive:\nLoose Clearcutter Blade Clearcutter Key\nExperience: 1,150\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Has the shredder been stopped, Dovahshark?","done":"All of Bloodhoof Village is in your debt this day. May the Earth Mother's grace stay with you always.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":53,"y":60.2,"n":"Morin Cloudstalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"94427":{"id":94427,"t":"A lesson in divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity.","desc":"A key tenant of being a paladin is the pursuit of divinity. This is not the pursuit of godhood, but merely the pursuit of good itself, for good's sake. We've all arrived at this place due to tragedy of one form or another, and it would be easy to lose that grace that defined us as paladins in life.\nGo to the Undercity and seek out Tanis Alderwood in the Trade Quarter. They are in need, and they could benefit greatly from some grace.","done":"You... you are a ‹class›? Please, do not hurt me. I-I know I'm not supposed to be panhandling. I have no quarrel with you or your order. Leave me be, I beg you!\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Danitha Morr","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":65.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Tanis Alderwood","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"1787":{"id":1787,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve a Defias Script from the Defias Rogue Wizards in Elwynn, and return to Gazin Tenorm in Stormwind.\nDefias Script Defias Rogue Wizard 50 %","desc":"We'll have time to talk more about the Symbol at a later time. What's important now is to get those papers we saw the Defias going over. If we can get our hands on them, we'll be able to prove the Defias have infiltrated Elwynn and hopefully gain some insight into what their plans are.\nI'm in no shape for battle as of now, ‹name›. Do you think you're strong enough to get those papers from the Defias here on the island?\nIf you're able to get them, bring them back to Gazin and let him know I'm all right.","rew":"Experience: 675","back":"Is Henze safe, ‹name›? Were you successful?\nBetween your skill with a weapon, and the power of the Light, I'd imagine Heroes' Vigil is safe from any Defias threat, but that's for the King and his advisors to say.","done":"Wonderful! You made it, and saved Henze. The Light is with you for sure, ‹name›!\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":72.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Henze Faulk","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":45,"n":"Gazin Tenorm","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5627":{"id":5627,"t":"Stars of Elune","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will learn: Starshards","done":"You've proven yourself worthy of Elune's attention, ‹name›. If you feel you're ready, I would very much like to teach you one of her spells unique to our people.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8827":{"id":8827,"t":"Winter's Presents","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Greatfather Winter. He is located near the Smokywood Pastures vendor area in Ironforge.","desc":"I hear Greatfather Winter - with the generous support of Smokywood Pastures - has put presents for everyone under the tree in Ironforge. I wish I could go, but I've got to look after the PX-238 Winter Wondervolt.\nBut you should definitely check it out. I'm sure Greatfather Winter has some presents with your name on them.","rew":"Experience: 10","done":"Oh, ho hello there! You can only be here for one reason: to open your Winter Veil presents.\nNow, don't you worry, Greatfather Winter hasn't forgotten about his favorite ‹race› ‹class›. Look under the tree and you'll find your gifts.\nDuring this season of giving, perhaps your friends would also enjoy receiving some of Smokeywood Pasture's excellent products?\nStormwind City Dun Morogh Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":67.9,"y":71.4,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":53.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Greatfather Winter","e":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.7,"y":73.5,"n":"Wonderform Operator","s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8507":{"id":8507,"t":"Field Duty","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report for duty at the Ironforge Brigade post near Hive'Zora. Prepare your Unsigned Field Duty Papers and obtain Signed Field Duty Papers from Captain Blackanvil and return to Windcaller Kaldon at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.\nNote: Healing or casting beneficial spells on a member of the Ironforge Brigade will flag you for PvP.\nSigned Field Duty Papers\nProvided: Unsigned Field Duty Papers","desc":"Greetings, ‹name›. Before I assign you to more involved tasks in the war, you'll need to do your share of field duty.\nYou will find Captain Blackanvil's Ironforge Brigade outside Hive'Zora.\nReport to him or his lieutenant, Janela Stouthammer and come back to me. I shall have a more advanced assignment for you ready.\nOh and please do us a favor and stay away from the Orgrimmar Legion. We've been forced to keep the two forces well apart from one another due to mutual animosity.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCombat Assignment Logistics Assignment Tactical Assignment\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You'll find Captain Blackanvil's force stationed outside Hive'Zora. Talk to his lieutenant, Janela Stouthammer, if you can't find him.","done":"Very well, ‹name› I've prepared a set of tasks that should make optimal use of your skills.\nWith the continued efforts of you and people like you, our enemy will soon be vanquished once and for all!\nShould you require a new mission briefing, return to Captain Blackanvil.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":50,"y":36.4,"n":"Windcaller Kaldon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"79947":{"id":79947,"t":"Geomancy the stone cold truth","lv":35,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Geomancy: The Stone-Cold Truth","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 280","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nGeomancy: The Stone-Cold Truth (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"81947":{"id":81947,"t":"Sanguine sorcery","lv":45,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Sanguine Sorcery","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 390","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nSanguine Sorcery (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"347":{"id":347,"t":"Rethban Ore","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 5 loads of Rethban Ore and bring it to Brother Paxton in the Northshire Library.\n5 Rethban Ore Redridge Drudger 33.8 % , Copper Vein 33 % , Tin Vein 33 %","desc":"Rethban Ore is named after the man who first found it, Bart Rethban. When smelted it's not as strong as iron, but its ore has a dark, flat color that some scribes use in their dyes. It can be found in the Rethban Caverns, north of here.\nWe usually have some in stock, but we're too busy preparing for Orc attacks to gather any. And besides...Redridge Gnolls are now living in the Rethban Caverns and their Drudgers are gathering the ore themselves.\nSo if you need some, you'll have to get it yourself.","rew":"Experience: 975\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Do you have the Rethban Ore?","done":"Oh, splendid! I can use this ore to make my dye, and then can finish copying The Stresses of Iron.\nThank you, ‹name›!\nRedridge Mountains Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":27.1,"y":48.6,"n":"Foreman Oslow","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.6,"y":40.4,"n":"Brother Paxton","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"3787":{"id":3787,"t":"Jonespyre's Request","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Quintis Jonespyre in Feathermoon Stronghold.","desc":"Excuse me, friend...\nA colleague of mine would like to speak with you about the research you are doing in conjunction with the Cenarion Circle. He is a druid by the name of Quintis Jonespyre, and he resides in Feathermoon Stronghold, Feralas. He would like to confer with you about morrowgrain... and he very much would like for you to keep our discussion from the ears of the Arch Druid.\nIf you're interested, speak with him; no doubt, all will be revealed once you do.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"I thank you for coming, weary traveler! Allow me to introduce myself - I am Quintis Jonespyre, druid and humble servant of Malfurion and the Cenarion Circle. My colleagues (General Shandris Feathermoon and the Protectorate - mayhap you've heard of us) and I wanted to talk with you about the work you are doing for Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.\nBefore we get much further, I'd like to ask that our discussion stay between just us. If you have no problem with this, then we may proceed.\nStormwind City Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":54.3,"y":84.1,"n":"Tannysa","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":32.4,"y":43.8,"n":"Quintis Jonespyre","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"187":{"id":187,"t":"Tiger Mastery","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ajeck Rouack of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Elder Stranglethorn Tigers.\nElder Stranglethorn Tiger slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Now I'm going to up the stakes on you and truly test your skill. Prove to me you can kill 10 Elder Stranglethorn Tigers. If you can do that, you will be ready for your final challenge before I declare you a master tiger hunter in Master Nesingwary's presence.\nElder Stranglethorn Tigers are not only the most difficult to find, they are also the fiercest to defeat.","rew":"Experience: 2,050","back":"You must kill 10 Elder Stranglethorn Tigers before I give you the final challenge that will determine if you are a true tiger hunting master.","done":"Most impressive. I believe you are almost ready.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.6,"y":10.6,"n":"Ajeck Rouack","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"587":{"id":587,"t":"Up to Snuff","lv":41,"min":37,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deeg in Booty Bay wants you to bring him 15 shares of Snuff.\n15 Snuff \"Pretty Boy\" Duncan 25 % , Bloodsail Warlock 25 % , Bloodsail Swashbuckler 25 % , Bloodsail Mage 25 % and 4 more","desc":"Ah, the sea life. I ain't gonna say it's the good life, but it's my life.\nWhen I get into port I like to find me a good bottle of grog and some high quality snuff. Nasty habits but what's a pirate without his vices, right?\nSo you can imagine how heartbroken I was to find out the herbalist here in town has gone and sold out of the stuff. Says his shipment got hijacked by those damned Bloodsail Raiders.\nI bet a fearless ‹class› like you could convince 'em to share the goods, eh?","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Any luck finding the goods, matey?","done":"Good show, ‹name›! And just before I need to ship out too! Can't thank you enough, old friend.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.3,"n":"Deeg","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1707":{"id":1707,"t":"Water Pouch Bounty","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Wastewander Water Pouches to Spigot Operator Luglunket in Gadgetzan.\n5 Wastewander Water Pouch Andre Firebeard 35 % , Wastewander Scofflaw 35 % , Wastewander Assassin 35 % , Wastewander Bandit 35 % and 3 more","desc":"Greetings ‹name› - the name's Luglunket, and we've got an important job for you if you're up for it! Huzzah!\nNothing would please me more as a seasoned spigot operator to take any Wastewander water pouches you might find out in the desert. That's our water anyway - the nomads have just stolen it is all! The Gadgetzan Water Company will offer you an official care package for every five you turn in. Most importantly though, you're helping Gadgetzan help itself!","rew":"You will receive:\nGadgetzan Water Co. Care Package\nExperience: 2,800\n+75 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Got the five Wastewander Water Pouches we need? If you do, then the Gadgetzan Water Company Care Package, Model 103-XB, will be yours!","done":"Excellent - the more water pouches we are able to reclaim, the further away from disaster we'll all be! Keep 'em coming, and I will be sure to reward you for every five water pouches you bring me.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.4,"n":"Spigot Operator Luglunket","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"4507":{"id":4507,"t":"Pawn Captures Queen","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat the Gorishi Hive Queen once she is summoned.\nBring the Gorishi Queen's Brain to Alchemist Pestlezugg in Gadgetzan.\nGorishi Queen Brain Gorishi Hive Queen\nProvided: Gorishi Queen Lure","desc":"Here's the lure. Inside the hive network should be a crystal of some sort. We think the silithid use the crystal as some sort of hive-wide attunement device. As for where this crystal might be, I'd say try the hatcheries inside the hive.\nUsing the lure on the crystal should roust out the queen, but be warned - she will probably be protected by several guards. Take out the queen and remove her brain. As icky as that sounds, we desperately need to study it. Good luck, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 5,450","back":"Acquiring the queen's brain for our research is absolutely imperative. From what we have learned, we believe that these silithid are quite possibly being controlled by a malign intelligence. I shudder to think what could control something as insidious as the silithid, ‹name›.","done":"Fantastic, ‹name›! We've won quite the victory here today. It will take some time for us to fully understand what we have here; we'll put it to good use though, don't you worry about that.\nAs for the silithid, I genuinely doubt that this was the full extent of their presence. This is much too clean of a resolution, I'm sorry to say.\nTanaris Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.9,"y":27,"n":"Alchemist Pestlezugg","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2747":{"id":2747,"t":"An Extraordinary Egg","lv":60,"min":42,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Extraordinary Egg","rew":"You will receive:\nBox of Goodies\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I have seen very few eggs retrieved from Feralas in extraordinary condition. These are eggs of the rarest sort...","done":"Well now, you have one--amazing!\nI hope you always remember the good you have done today.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.4,"y":26.9,"n":"Curgle Cranklehop","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8587":{"id":8587,"t":"Return to Narain","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the 500 Pound Chicken to Narain Soothfancy in Tanaris.\n500 Pound Chicken\nProvided: 500 Pound Chicken","desc":"I'm a goblin of my word, kid. Here's your 500 pound chicken.\nWhat a gnome wants with a 500 pound chicken, I'll never know...\n<Dirge grumbles something unintelligible.>\nProbably to sleep in it... Dirty gnomes...","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"What is that scrumptious smell?","done":"<Narain mashes two fists into the huge chicken, stuffing his face full of Dirge's delicious delicacy.>\nMMmmm... This is unbelievable! Best chicken I've ever had!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.6,"y":28.1,"n":"Dirge Quikcleave","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8747":{"id":8747,"t":"The Path of the Protector","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"Impressive, little one. You have gone through much trouble to gain the favor of the Bronze Flight. Your dedication is noted.\nThe signet ring of the protector will offer superior protection against the forces of evil.\nBe warned, once you have chosen your path, you will have no recourse should you change your mind.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"907":{"id":907,"t":"Enraged Thunder Lizards","lv":18,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Thunder Lizard Blood to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo.\n3 Thunder Lizard Blood Stormhide 80 % , Thunderhead 80 % , Stormsnout 80 %","desc":"Now, ‹name›, you must face the great thunder lizards. So large are the beasts, the ground rumbles as they stomp across the plains. Take care as you fight them, for one false step and you may find yourself beneath their feet.\nYou will find the thunder lizards in the southern Barrens. They are known as Stormsnouts, Stormhides and Thunderheads. Return to me after you have bested them.","rew":"Experience: 1,700\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Are the thunder lizards defeated, ‹name›?","done":"It is good to see you return with proof of victory. And it is good to know you have done so with your bones unbroken.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"5147":{"id":5147,"t":"Wanted - Arnak Grimtotem","lv":29,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Arnak Grimtotem and bring proof of your deed to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post.\nArnak's Hoof Arnak Grimtotem","desc":"Wanted: Arnak Grimtotem\nArnak the outcast is wanted for the heinous crimes of murder and kidnapping. Handsome rewards will be given to those brave enough to bring this criminal to justice.\nArnak was last seen on the cliffs near the Darkcloud Pinnacle. Show the proof of your deed to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post in order to claim the reward.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBrawnhide Armor Plainsguard Leggings\nExperience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you any news of that murderous Arnak Grimtotem?","done":"Hah! Well, this is excellent news! I was starting to think that he would never be brought to justice!\nHere you are, ‹name›... and thanks. News of Anrak's foul deeds boiled my blood!","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":46,"y":50.9,"n":"Wanted Poster - Arnak Grimtotem","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":45.7,"y":50.7,"n":"Cliffwatcher Longhorn","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1147":{"id":1147,"t":"The Swarm Grows","lv":35,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 5 Silithid Searchers, 5 Silithid Hive Drones, and 5 Silithid Invaders and return to Moktar Krin in Thousand Needles.\nSilithid Searcher slain : 0/ 5\nSilithid Hive Drone slain : 0/ 5\nSilithid Invader slain : 0/ 5","desc":"Hmm. Seems Belgrom thinks those monsters are a threat. He wants them pushed back into whatever depths they crawled up out of.\nI guess killing the dwarves sent by the Explorers' League wasn't enough--now I have to send a half-dead war party into another battle. We won't be able to do it ourselves; not while we're in this condition. The dig site's to the south of here. There shouldn't be anymore dwarves to deal with. Feel up to wielding a blade or staff and doing your part to aid us?","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"With the amount of travelers heading out to the Flats for those races, I'm sure we can convince enough adventure seekers to help push back those insects. My party and I won't be able to leave until we do.","done":"Ha! That ichor you're covered in actually makes you prettier, ‹name›! It certainly does make you reek at the same time though. Don't stand too close to the kodo; you'll either start a stampede or cause them to go into heat.\nI think my companions would agree that your smell alone is proof you've done your part to help us against those insect creatures. Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":67.6,"y":63.9,"n":"Moktar Krin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1067":{"id":1067,"t":"Return to Thunder Bluff","lv":23,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Lydon's Toxin to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff.\nLydon's Toxin\nProvided: Lydon's Toxin","desc":"Here is the toxin. If you use it against the Venture Company it should produce favorable, perhaps even contagious, results. I must say, it is quite exciting to see my work applied in the field!\nBut before using it, take it to Apothecary Zamah. She must create a delivery method for the toxin to maximize its effect.","rew":"Experience: 1,400\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"You have returned, ‹name›. Do you bring aid from Apothecary Lydon?","done":"A toxin from Apothecary Lydon? Very good. If I know Lydon, then this toxin will be quite effective against the Venture Company...\nHillsbrad Foothills Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":22.8,"y":20.9,"n":"Apothecary Zamah","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"427":{"id":427,"t":"At War With The Scarlet Crusade","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Executor Zygand of Brill wants you to kill 10 Scarlet Warriors.\nScarlet Warrior slain : 0/ 10","desc":"The documents Executor Arren provided are just the break we needed in our battle with the wretched Scarlet Crusade. We now know their exact locations throughout Tirisfal Glades.\nBut the Deathguard has larger concerns. The Lich King's army grows in number each night. We need someone with \"initiative\" like yourself to drive the Scarlet Crusade to the grave.\nProve to me you are capable of serving The Dark Lady by travelling west to the tower past the Solliden Farmstead and slay 10 Scarlet Warriors.","rew":"Money: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"If you wish to prove your worth to The Dark Lady, slay 10 Scarlet Warriors, ‹class›.","done":"Most excellent, ‹class›. Your skill in the art of combat is undeniable.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.6,"y":51.8,"n":"Executor Zygand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"7627":{"id":7627,"t":"Wheel of the Black March","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Large Brilliant Shards and 25 Dark Iron Ore to Gorzeeki in the Burning Steppes.\n6 Large Brilliant Shard\n25 Dark Iron Ore Dark Iron Deposit , Warbringer Construct 13.4 % , Wrath Hammer Construct 13 % , Ragereaver Golem 13 % and 4 more","desc":"A Wheel of the Black March contains and directs the violent energies required for the Circle of Greater Summoning. For Gozeeki to construct a wheel, he will need both large brilliant shards from an enchanter, and dark iron ore from a master miner.\nAcquire these and bring them to my servant.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"The Wheel of the Black March isn't easy to make, and takes a lot of materials. Have you gathered them yet?","done":"There they are! I hear that dark iron ore is only found in the depths of Blackrock, and I'm sure these shards weren't easy to find either. I am often awed at the dedication you warlocks have. If you instead bent all that energy into the art of bug catching, oh... such a feast you would enjoy!\nSorry, a small digression. I'll create the wheel and keep it for you until you're ready for your ritual.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.7,"y":31.6,"n":"Mor'zul Bloodbringer","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Gorzeeki Wildeyes","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"8427":{"id":8427,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"4987":{"id":4987,"t":"Glyphed Oaken Branch","lv":56,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Based on the magic enchanted within the Glyphed Oaken Branch, its delivery to the Cenarion Circle in Thunder Bluff is the next step the tauren druid sought. Seek one of the druids there for assistance.\nGlyphed Oaken Branch\nProvided: Glyphed Oaken Branch","desc":"The lifeless hand of the tauren druid clutches a surprisingly healthy looking oaken branch. Examining the branch reveals glyphs of a druidic nature carved into the bark.\nAs you grasp the branch, you notice it is warm to the touch, more than it should be. The image of Thunder Bluff in Mulgore enters your mind - Elder Rise specifically - and the words \"Cenarion Circle\" are on the tip of your tongue. It would appear that the suggestion of where to take the branch has been placed within it.","rew":"You will receive:\nCerise Drape\nExperience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"On behalf of the Cenarion Circle, I bid you welcome to this enclave, ‹class›. What business do you have with us?","done":"This is from Mulgris, you say? We had heard he sought to minister to the creatures suffering in the Plaguelands, but this is most unexpected... and most saddening. Mulgris is... was a good friend. I will mourn his passing deeply.\nHis efforts have not gone in vain, thanks to your diligence. In this branch, much lore is stored about the plague the Scourge propagates upon the land. We will study it diligently. As for you, please accept this. It is the least we can do for your noble efforts.\nWestern Plaguelands Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":53.7,"y":64.7,"n":"Mulgris Deepriver","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":75.6,"y":31.6,"n":"Nara Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5227":{"id":5227,"t":"Gahrron's Withering Cauldron","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Arcane Quickener sold by Alchemist Arbington , sold by Apothecary Dithers\n4 Ectoplasmic Resonator Hungering Wraith 50 % , Spectral Attendant 50 % , Screaming Haunt 50 % , Haunting Vision 50 % and 4 more\n4 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 625\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air. A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform.\nHaving already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.","done":"Adding the reagents to the cauldron's mix begins to change the color and texture of the cloud it spews forth. Scourge that are even remotely near the cauldron appear to recoil at the introduction of the new components into the environment.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":62.5,"y":58.5,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92747":{"id":92747,"t":"Moonbrook espionage","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 8 Suspicious Industrial Supplies from Moonbrook.\n8 Suspicious Industrial Supplies","desc":"Strange - the poison does not seem to originate from the mines you investigated.\nI am told the Deadmines under the town of Moonbrook are the largest, deepest mines of Westfall, but they have been abandoned since the First War. Could the Deadmines be active again?\nPlease travel to Moonbrook, ‹name›, and look for evidence of mining or industrial activity. This is the last lead we have!","back":"Did you find anything?","done":"What is all this?","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":52.4,"y":53,"n":"Alba Fairmoon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"5067":{"id":5067,"t":"Leggings of Arcana","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 50. Pays -50g instead of 0.","obj":"In order to create the Leggings of Arcana, you will be required to bring the following items back to Malyfous Darkhammer: 1 Pristine Hide of the Beast; 5 Frayed Abomination Stitchings; 5 Arcanite Bars; 5 Frostwhisper's Embalming Fluid.\nYou will also be required to pay 50 gold pieces for the crafting of the item.\nItem #12731\n5 Frayed Abomination Stitching\n5 Arcanite Bar\n5 Frostwhisper's Embalming Fluid\nRequired money: 50","desc":"While the crafting of such an item has never successfully been accomplished, it is thought to be possible - under the right circumstance.\nShould the seeker of arcanum desire to imbue leggings with immense power, the following they must find:\n* The pristine hide of the Beast.\n* Frayed abomination stitchings.\n*Arcanite Bars.\n*Frostwhisper's embalming fluid.\nBEHOLD!","rew":"You will receive:\nLeggings of Arcana","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61,"y":38.8,"n":"Malyfous's Catalogue","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":61,"y":38.8,"n":"Malyfous Darkhammer","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"8187":{"id":8187,"t":"Falcon's Call","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring me thise things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!\nPrimal Hakkari Idol\nPunctured Voodoo Doll\nPrimal Hakkari Idol Jin'do the Hexxer in Zul'Gurub , Bloodlord Mandokir in Zul'Gurub\nPunctured Voodoo Doll Gurubashi Headhunter 0.1 % in Zul'Gurub , Voodoo Slave 0.1 % in Zul'Gurub , Zulian Cub 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Zulian Tiger 0 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"Zanza can create the ancient troll enchantments with the right components. The first is a primal Hakkari idol that must be taken from the most powerful of the Hakkari lieutenants: Jin'do and the Bloodlord.\nThe second is a punctured voodoo doll. These can be found in the piles of refuse that litter this foul place. Look inside the jinxed hoodoo.\nBring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nFalcon's Call\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Bring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","done":"Use it well, ‹class›. Show the Hakkari no mercy!\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8187","cats":["zulgurub"]},"8107":{"id":8107,"t":"Kezan's Taint","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Kezan's Taint","rew":"You will receive:\nKezan's Taint\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Honor is earned amongst the Zandalar trolls, ‹name›. With honor comes reward - friendship, alliance...\nHand me the talisman so that I may enhance its power.","done":"Draw from the darkness, ‹class›. Embrace the shadows. Let Kezan's Taint supplement your dark meddling.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});